WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.167
-Hasan Minhaj, it is always great to see you.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.634
Welcome back to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:05.834
How's it going, pal?

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:08.067
-It's rough. [ Laughter ]

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.167
-Talk to me. What do you mean? Talk to me.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:13.200
-I'm not doing good. -Wow. Wow. Why? Why?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.834
-This show is bad luck.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:16.868
[ Laughter ] -Our -- This show is?

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:20.234
-Every time I come on this show, Jimmy,

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.567
I'm embroiled in some controversy.

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.067
[ Laughter ] -Some con-trov-ersy?

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:25.701
-Yes, last time I was on the show...

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:28.234
-Yes -- -...I did a couple jokes

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.501
and I pissed off doctors of osteopathic medicine.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.767
-Ooh. -A niche group of physicians.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.167
They were hate-tweeting the show from their Teslas.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.801
-Ohh. That sounds terri--

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.701
-And...

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:40.901
[ Laughter ] -Oh, no.

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:43.667
-This past week, I was on "Celebrity Jeopardy!",

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.033
and now fans of "Jeopardy!" hate my guts.

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:47.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.400
I have this unique power to piss off dedicated nerds.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:56.300
-I heard something about this "Celebrity Jeopardy!" thing.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.434
-Okay, so, I was on "Celebrity Jeopardy!"

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.467
And I was raising money for charity.

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:03.601
[ Cheers and applause ] Yes, I'm a good person.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.501
-"I'm a good person." -I'm raising money

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:07.501
for International Relief Commiteee, which is --

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:10.000
raising money for victims of the floods in Pakistan.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.133
Yeah, yeah. I'm a good guy.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.968
[ Cheers and applause ] -Sure.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:18.400
-And I'm playing the show, and -- and I'm passionate.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.267
-What do you mean? What does passionate mean?

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:23.133
-I was just playing with vigor and passion.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.567
-Well, let me just show everyone the clip.

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.901
We'll decide if "passionate" is the word.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.133
Let's take a look.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.934
-Uh -- What is [Shouting] -That's time!

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.067
-Hasan.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.701
-What is, I plead the Fifth? -That's correct.

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:36.667
The Fifth Amendment. -A little swag on it.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:39.901
What is...guts? -No.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.801
-Hasan. -What is cardinal?

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.701
-Yes. -All gas, no brakes!

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:45.801
What is Ireland? -That's correct.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:48.434
-Oh, ho, ho! And I guessed that!

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:49.634
-Hasan.

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:52.167
-Oh, no! What is a redshirt?

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.501
-That is correct. -Wow.

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:56.934
[ Laughter ] -Why did you --

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:58.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:01.334
-Yeah! -Getting in people's faces?

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:05.534
What was going on -- -I was -- I was into it.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:08.467
And if you get it right, yeah, hang on the rim.

00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:09.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.634
-You don't hang on the rim if you dunk the ball, no.

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:13.234
-The fans weren't having it.

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:14.834
-Let me just read a couple tweets, if you don't mind,

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.167
from fans of "Jeopardy!"

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.834
-Oh, geez. Jimmy.

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:27.434
They @'d you, by the way, which I always love.

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:29.467
-I know, rocketdan7. Geez.

00:02:29.467 --> 00:02:31.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.767
-This one's from @lazyfelter. They said...

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:43.801
Wow. No. This is good that people get -- they say this.

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:46.934
Here. This is by -- Big Thankful Dad said...

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:55.501
That's Big Thankful Dad. This is a big thankful dad.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:57.400
-Yeah, yeah, but he's being a mean dad right now.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.334
-No. He's being thankful. He's thankful.

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:02.200
This person said...

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.567
And then this is from TV Insider --

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:10.734
-Okay, okay, well, first of all,

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:12.634
I'm not cool enough to do cocaine, okay?

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:13.934
-That's not a cool thing.

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:16.000
-Everything you hate about me is who I really am.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.167
[ Laughter ] -Oh, my.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.534
[ Audience awws ] Don't feel bad for him yet.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:21.000
Hold on. This is the best.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.601
TV Insider, which I follow. I love TV Insider.

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.968
-Oh, geez. -I trust their opinion.

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:27.667
And they say, "'Celebrity Jeopardy!' fans

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:31.234
call Hasan Minhaj 'most annoying' contestant ever."

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:32.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:33.634
Congratulations.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:37.133
-That one hurt because, you know,

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:40.734
the -- the show's been on for over 58 years.

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:42.534
[ Laughter ] -Don't let it --

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:45.200
-And they've had 15,000 contestants on the show.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.601
-Who cares about numbers?

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.467
-And Dr. Oz was a contestant on --

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:49.667
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:51.667
-Don't get into -- -No, no, no. Jimmy.

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:54.667
You know what? Maybe my dad was wrong.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.868
He said I'd never break records on that show.

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:58.667
[ Laughter ] -You did.

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:01.200
-You know what? Listen, Jimmy.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.367
I'm in the eye of the storm.

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:05.133
-Wow. -And I can't take it anymore.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:08.567
So I want to apologize to the fans of "Jeopardy!"

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:10.868
Where's my camera? Here? -Sure.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:13.400
[ Laughter ] Your camera.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.200
-I've been journaling and writing about this.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.100
To the fans of "Jeopardy!"...

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:22.334
I want to take this moment to apologize.

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:23.901
"Jeopardy!" fans, look at me.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.868
[ Laughter ] -Oh, my goodness.

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:29.667
-I'm sorry I desecrated an American institution.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:32.601
I'm sorry I ripped your 7:00 p.m. linear TV pacifier

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.434
out of your geriatric mouth.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:36.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.367
And most importantly, I'm sorry for trying

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:41.968
to make "Jeopardy!" fun.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:45.467
-What are you doing?!

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:53.300
-Now, what I'm about to say to you...

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.434
is something I've said to my wife a thousand times.

00:04:57.434 --> 00:05:00.334
This is not an excuse.

00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:01.968
This is an explanation.

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:04.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:08.133
Let me explain my behavior.

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:11.100
When you're playing "Jeopardy!" at home in your sweats

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.467
and you're confident and you got --

00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:17.200
you're playing with the shampoo or the remote...

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.968
-Yeah.

00:05:18.968 --> 00:05:21.968
...you think you're the [bleep].

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:25.300
But you don't know what that game does to you in the arena.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.934
So I walk in -- Jimmy, don't even laugh.

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:32.334
This is not funny. "TVinsider.com."

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:34.534
You don't even know what Uproxx said about me.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:35.934
-I don't want to -- It's "Uproxx" with two X's.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:37.601
-Yeah.

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:39.734
-So...

00:05:39.734 --> 00:05:40.968
You go -- No, listen.

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:42.167
You go in. -Okay.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:45.501
-You go in to the studio, Culver City, Sony lot.

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:47.534
You walk in, and you see --

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:49.767
you feel the history of, you know, Alex Trebek Studios.

00:05:49.767 --> 00:05:51.234
-It's historic.

00:05:51.234 --> 00:05:53.868
-And you can smell the history and the asbestos and...

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:56.534
And you look around and you're like, "This is it?"

00:05:56.534 --> 00:05:59.033
It's kind of like when your dad goes to any American airport.

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:01.734
They're like, "Really? This is --

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:03.434
This is why China's winning."

00:06:03.434 --> 00:06:05.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:07.167
Then the producer comes in, right?

00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:08.868
And they sit you down, and they're very --

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:11.033
They have buzzer technique. This is a big deal.

00:06:11.033 --> 00:06:12.434
"Jeopardy!" fans, you know this, right?

00:06:12.434 --> 00:06:14.400
And I know this. I've seen the videos.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:17.534
And I go, "Listen. The buzzer's janky.

00:06:17.534 --> 00:06:20.100
My buzzer is janky." And I told the producer this.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.934
I go, "I know all the techniques.

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:24.334
Up above, right? Sideways. Gunslinger. I know this.

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:27.901
But my buzzer is messed up, so I'm going to hold it up here

00:06:27.901 --> 00:06:31.033
so everyone can see this on camera."

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:33.400
I'm telling you. I did it. That was my strategy.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.300
-We have the tape. Let's check out...

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.901
-Show them the tape. -...the buzzer game tape.

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:39.634
Keep an eye on Hasan trying to buzz in.

00:06:39.634 --> 00:06:41.334
Take a look. -Look at my hand.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.400
-Wil? -What is "Rugrats"?

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.334
-That's right.

00:06:45.334 --> 00:06:46.901
Troian. -Who is Cardi B?

00:06:46.901 --> 00:06:50.033
-Yes. Wil. -What is a gargoyle?

00:06:50.033 --> 00:06:52.400
-Wil? -What is South Carolina?

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.133
-Wil. -Who is Dakota Johnson?

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.467
-Yes. Wil.

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:57.501
-Who are Billy Ray Cyrus and Miley Cyrus?

00:06:57.501 --> 00:06:59.133
-Wil. -What is McDonald's?

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:01.767
-Yes. -That is proof! That is proof!

00:07:01.767 --> 00:07:03.734
That is -- That's not fair! That is proof!

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:05.634
-History will vindicate me. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:08.467
Now, look, while I'm there, I'm telling Mayim.

00:07:08.467 --> 00:07:12.133
I go, "Mayim, my clicker, my buzzer! I'm buzzing in!"

00:07:12.133 --> 00:07:15.400
She goes, "Your buzzer's fine." I go, "You're gaslighting me."

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.734
She goes, "No, I'm not."

00:07:16.734 --> 00:07:18.901
I go, "You're victim-blaming now."

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:20.434
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.434 --> 00:07:22.567
Now, look. Here's the thing. -Yeah.

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:26.701
-You may be wondering, "Hasan, why are you being a psycho?"

00:07:26.701 --> 00:07:28.567
It's not my fault.

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:30.834
Because...

00:07:30.834 --> 00:07:34.400
"Jeopardy!" is like American elections.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.968
Right?

00:07:35.968 --> 00:07:37.400
Winner-take-all.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.501
There is no second or third place.

00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:43.601
So it incentivizes bad behavior.

00:07:43.601 --> 00:07:45.467
If you're second or third,

00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:47.534
you gotta give all the other contestants the smoke.

00:07:47.534 --> 00:07:50.567
I'm sorry. I gotta kamikaze-mission you.

00:07:50.567 --> 00:07:53.400
So I started taunting the other people I was competing against,

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.133
making fun of them. -Yeah.

00:07:55.133 --> 00:07:56.801
-And I'm gaining. Right?

00:07:56.801 --> 00:07:59.067
And I'm like, "Just get to Double Jeopardy!, and it's on.

00:07:59.067 --> 00:08:00.300
You're back in the game."

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.868
-Yeah, you can always make a comeback.

00:08:01.868 --> 00:08:03.200
-Yes, and I got to Double Jeopardy!

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:05.267
-That's right. You did. Can I ask --

00:08:05.267 --> 00:08:06.734
Can I tell everyone the answer?

00:08:06.734 --> 00:08:08.968
And then you could tell me what your question was?

00:08:08.968 --> 00:08:10.467
-Fine.

00:08:10.467 --> 00:08:13.400
"-A chapter no one ever wants to read.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:16.801
This one is often called a reorganization bankruptcy.

00:08:16.801 --> 00:08:18.601
Like JCPenney in 2020."

00:08:18.601 --> 00:08:19.834
-Okay.

00:08:19.834 --> 00:08:21.200
-Okay. How much did you bet, first of all?

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.000
-Everything.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:30.133
I said chapter 7 bankruptcy, which is liquidity bankruptcy.

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:32.067
But the answer was chapter 11,

00:08:32.067 --> 00:08:34.067
which is reorganization bankruptcy.

00:08:34.067 --> 00:08:35.601
-Chapter 7? That's the famous chapter.

00:08:35.601 --> 00:08:37.367
-I know!

00:08:37.367 --> 00:08:39.400
-No one knows chapter 7! Liquidity?!

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:42.634
-So I got chapter 11 wrong, and chapter 7 bankrupted me!

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:44.367
I had to liquidate all my assets.

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:45.534
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:08:45.534 --> 00:08:47.734
-So you got chapter 11 from chapter 7.

00:08:47.734 --> 00:08:49.133
-Yeah.

00:08:49.133 --> 00:08:51.000
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.467
-Yeah, Jimmy.

00:08:52.467 --> 00:08:56.334
-Well, did you learn anything from this whole ordeal?

00:08:56.334 --> 00:08:58.767
-Yeah, I've been reflecting.

00:08:58.767 --> 00:09:01.767
You know, TV is all about expectations,

00:09:01.767 --> 00:09:03.234
and life is about expectations.

00:09:03.234 --> 00:09:06.267
And when people watch "Jeopardy!",

00:09:06.267 --> 00:09:11.000
they want to see a cerebral, quiet quiz show.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.033
But I need to go to a place where I'm celebrated.

00:09:13.033 --> 00:09:14.534
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.534 --> 00:09:17.467
I need to go to a place where the unhinged are accepted.

00:09:17.467 --> 00:09:18.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:18.868 --> 00:09:21.801
Where the eccentric are allowed.

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:25.000
Where cocaine consumption is encouraged.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.367
[ Laughter ]

00:09:26.367 --> 00:09:31.434
Jimmy, that is why next summer, I, Hasan Minhaj,

00:09:31.434 --> 00:09:34.868
will be taking my talents to "The Price is Right."

00:09:34.868 --> 00:09:36.067
-Whoa!

00:09:36.067 --> 00:09:38.033
-I'm going on "The Price is Right"!

00:09:38.033 --> 00:09:39.467
-Hasan Minhaj!

00:09:39.467 --> 00:09:42.100
"The King's Jester" is streaming now on Netflix!

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.734
